he body; => nil or {:yin.k/kind k :yin.k/path p …}\n424:| E2 | **`E` is the free environment under the lexical chain.** With `C = (set (mapcat params (chain (body pc))))` the lexically bound names at that pc (a return frame's chain is that of its own `pc`): (a) **every name of `C` is a key of `bindings`**, a nil binding being a present key (`bind-params` nil-fills, so a lexical name is never absent; an absent one would be nil-filled on lower and break the canonical round trip); (b) `(apply dissoc bindings C) = (apply dissoc (:free-env task) C)` as maps of `V`: a key outside `C` the free environment lacks, a free key `E` lacks, or a differing value, is a defect | `:free-env-mismatch` |\n549:(`dest nil`, `live []`): `A` and the relative `site = site-pc` as in 1-2\n570:`:pc = off + site + 1`; `:regs []`; `:live []`; `:dest nil`;\n571:`:resume-mode :return-result`; `:frames []` and `:store-of nil`\n654:`(mapv Wᵢ (stack-layout_{Aᵢ} (dec pcᵢ)))`, then `slice(current) =\n655:(mapv W (stack-layout (dec pc)))`; `:continuation` = for each `fᵢ`\n692::stack (concat of the K slices, in order) :frames [] :store-of nil\n726:duplicates, nil-fill and extra-argument dropping, which are\n746:free-env  := the root's free-env row (never derived from any E)\n747:F[i]      := (mapv #(get E %) params(cᵢ))      for i = 0 … j\n849:| 21 | **free-env shadowing** (the review's row) | initial free env `{x 99}`; `(let1 f (fn [] x) ((fn [x] (f (next-of c))) 1))` | append `\"B\"` | act, `:next`; `E` at the read binds `x` to 1; root `free-env` carries `x 99` | the lowered `f` returns `99` (not nil, not 1) on every lane; **the one row the earlier design would have failed** | yes |\n850:| 22 | nil-valued live register | `(let1 pair (fn [p q] (cat (cat [] p) q)) (pair nil (next-of c)))`: the `nil` operand is evaluated **before** the read and is live across it (`(cat nil (next-of c))` would give `(conj nil \"B\")`, the list `(\"B\")`, so a vector-building `pair` is used; there is no `vector` primitive, 